# AGENTS.md — `workflow/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies. Human orientation is in
[`README.md`](README.md).

## Additional constraints

- Rules declare all inputs, outputs, parameters, logs, and execution
  environments. No undeclared side-effect writes.
- `workflow/scripts/` is Snakemake-only adaptation: read declared inputs/config,
  call tested `src/` behavior, and write only declared outputs. Algorithms belong
  in `src/`; operator workflows belong in top-level `scripts/`.
- Select datasets by a key resolved from `conf/catalog.yaml`; do not repeat their
  paths in workflow configuration or code.
- Route outputs by lifecycle: disposable scratch to `data/interim/`, reusable
  analysis-ready datasets to `data/processed/`, and terminal QC/figures/report
  tables to `results/`. Never write to `data/raw/`.
- Scientific values come from `conf/config.yaml`; DAG selectors from
  `workflow/config.yaml`; executor resources from `workflow/profiles/`.
- No silent fallback, implicit data correction, undeclared sample dropping, or
  success without required QC/provenance artifacts.

## Before completion

```bash
snakemake -n <target>
snakemake --cores 1 <target>
```

Confirm the target appears in the DAG, outputs are in canonical homes and
ignored/DVC-backed as required, raw inputs are unchanged, and
`results/provenance.json` names the actual inputs, configuration, code,
environment, and generated artifacts.
